{
  "about": [
    "What the drawn values say, as lists. scene.mjs is handed this file and reads its words, its boxes and an icon's shapes by it: a property is said because it stands here, and nothing is said that does not.",
    "Every property the pinned browser computes (getComputedStyle of an element, enumerated) stands in this file once: on a list, under `elsewhere` when another reading of the tool holds it, or under `notListed` with the reason. paint-properties.test.ts asks the browser and fails on a name this file does not know, so a new browser brings its new properties here before it draws a picture.",
    "A row: `property`; `source`, the specification whose property table names it (a key of `sources`); `initial`, its computed value on an element nothing styled (`currentcolor` where it follows the words' colour). A row is said only where its computed value is not that, so a plain thing says nothing; `said: always` marks the few that are a type's own values.",
    "`as` names the reading that says the property when that is not its own name (a border's three values a side are one `border`). `with` names the listed property that must itself be said at the same box for this one to paint anything. `when` names a condition scene.mjs knows; one it does not know is refused.",
    "Words, `from`: where the value is read. A property a child inherits is read on the element the words stand in (no `from`). `line`: on the box that lays out their line, for a property that is the line's and no child inherits. `around`: on every box of the line around the words. `decorating`: on every box around the words that draws a line under, over or through them, as far out as the browser passes such a line in: an ancestor's line is drawn through its descendants' words though their own computed value says none."
  ],
  "browser": "Chromium as @playwright/test pins it (tolerance.json `playwright`), started with tolerance.json's `chromiumArgs`",
